# SET-PIECE (M18 phase 0): the ladder shelf.
#
# A two-unit cliff with two ladders up it and a heart on the shelf above. The
# piece is also a CLIMB -- `piece_exit = 2` -- so the generator carries on from
# two units higher, exactly as it would after a ramp.
#
# ONE LADDER, AND THE QUEUE IS THE POINT. The first draft used two, on the
# reasoning that a queue is four players standing still in a game whose threat
# model is being moved somewhere you did not choose. Overruled at playtest, and
# rightly: a queue is not dead time, it is an ORDER — who climbs first, who
# holds the ground below, who is last and most exposed. Two ladders delete that
# decision to save three seconds.
#
# It also makes the shelf a place the party is briefly split across two heights,
# which is the only moment this piece has.
#
# NOTHING THAT SHOOTS AT THE TOP, deliberately. A climber has no verbs -- no
# dodge, no dash, no cover -- which is the same argument that got hazards banned
# from beside a lift in M17 phase 9, and it was learned there from a playtest that
# read as "the elevator hurts you". The reward for the climb is the heart; the
# cost is the time, and the time is paid somewhere you cannot answer back.
#
# Cover on the shelf, because the piece AFTER this one does not know it is being
# stamped behind a climb and may well point something down at the landing.

name = piece_ladder_shelf
base_height = 0
width = 21
length = 6
piece_exit = 2
tags = foot, piece, quiet

